    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-agricultural-education-bf9643-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Agricultural Education BF9643",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Agricultural Education BF9643 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Assistant Professor of Agricultural Education BF9643 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Agricultural Education BF9643 Apply Now Assistant Professor of Agricultural Education BF9643 495284 Stillwater DIV AGRICULTRL SCI & NATURAL RESRCS (STW) Faculty PhD Assistant Professor of Agricultural Education POSITION DESCRIPTION This is an 11-month, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, funded 75% Instruction and 25% Oklahoma Agricultural Experiment Station (OAES). The start date is negotiable. MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate for this position is expected to provide leadership in teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in agricultural education, develop a research line of inquiry in the OAES, and contribute to the outreach and service missions of the department. This faculty member will: (a) Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in agricultural education, delivered on campus and online, for the agricultural teacher preparation program and agricultural education, more broadly defined; (b) Lead various Curriculum for Agricultural Science Education (CASE) Initiatives, (c) Recruit, advise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students; (d) Supervise student teaching interns; (e) Contribute to the scholarship of the profession through innovative teaching approaches, research, curriculum development, external grants/contracts, and other forms of scholarly effort; (f) Develop a strong research program in agricultural teacher education with an emphasis on integration of science, math and other core academic areas; (g) Conduct appropriate service activities on and off campus. The Department of Agricultural Education, Communications and Leadership at Oklahoma State University has developed a strong reputation for being a national leader in delivering CASE trainings. Therefore, the successful candidate will be expected to become CASE certified in various curricular areas to deliver course content to pre-service and in-service teachers. In addition, the successful candidate will develop and assess the impacts of teachers, teacher development, curriculum, FFA engagement, SAE projects, and other aspects of the program on students’ knowledge, efficacy, and career choices across various career pathways in agricultural food, fiber, and natural resources industries. QUALIFICATIONS The successful candidate must have a doctorate in agricultural education or a closely related discipline. Doctoral degree candidates are welcome to apply but must have completed their degree before beginning employment. Applicants must have at least three years professional experience as a school-based agricultural education teacher and demonstrated excellence in teaching, including the ability to deliver courses using distance education technologies. Candidates for the position must show promise for carrying out research and other forms of scholarship that contribute to the discipline of agricultural education. SALARY AND BENEFITS Salary and benefits are competitive based on qualifications and experience. Retirement and long-term disability, medical, dental and life insurance programs are available to employees. Continuation of this position is subject to performance, needs and available funding. ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT The department’s undergraduate programs are organized into three majors: agricultural education, agricultural communications, and agricultural leadership. Graduate degrees offered include the Master of Agriculture, Master of Science in Agricultural Education and Leadership, Master of Science in Agricultural Communications, and Doctor of Philosophy in Agricultural Education, Communications and Leadership. Approximately 500 students are enrolled in undergraduate and graduate programs in the department. The department is one of nine academic departments within the Ferguson College of Agriculture. For more information about the department, visit our website: http://aged.okstate.edu/. Oklahoma State University is an 1862 Land-Grant Institution with approximately 24,000 students on the Stillwater campus. The University was founded as the Oklahoma Territorial Agricultural and Mechanical College on Christmas Day 1890. Stillwater, located in North Central Oklahoma, is one of the fastest growing areas in the state and is consistently listed among the most desirable and safest places to live in the United States. For further information about the Oklahoma State University system and the Stillwater campus, visit the University’s website: http://okstate.edu/. APPLICATION PROCEDURE AND DEADLINES To apply, a candidate should submit: (a) a letter of application describing how their academic preparation and experience qualify them for this faculty position; (b) curriculum vitae; (c) statement describing their teaching philosophy and research focus; (d) transcripts from their degree granting institutions; and (e) names, complete addresses, e-mail addresses, and telephone numbers of three professional references. Questions can be directed to: Dr. Bradley M. Coleman Assistant Professor, Agricultural Education, Communications and Leadership Oklahoma State University 238 Agricultural Hall Stillwater, OK 74078 P: 405-744-2073 E: b.coleman@okstate.edu Review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026, and will continue until a qualified candidate is selected. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 386f4ce1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) a4d06019 Last Name (required) f4ac67fc Email (required) 2e754eb0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 3534f23e Last Name (required) 0a0d257d Email (required) 92d0aa39 Save this job for later c6b96dff Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System