    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-prof-and-state-extension-vegetable-specialist-bf9549-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Prof and State Extension Vegetable Specialist BF9549",
      "description": "Assistant Prof and State Extension Vegetable Specialist BF9549 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Assistant Prof and State Extension Vegetable Specialist BF9549 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Prof and State Extension Vegetable Specialist BF9549 Apply Now Assistant Prof and State Extension Vegetable Specialist BF9549 495279 Stillwater DIV AGRICULTRL SCI & NATURAL RESRCS (STW) Faculty PhD Assistant Professor and State Extension Vegetable Specialist Vegetable Production Systems Department of Horticulture and Landscape Architecture Division of Agricultural Sciences and Natural Resources Oklahoma State University Description: The Department of Horticulture and Landscape Architecture at Oklahoma State University (OSU) invites applications for a full-time, eleven-month, tenure-track faculty position as Assistant Professor and State Extension Vegetable Specialist in vegetable production systems. This position carries an appointment of 75% Extension and 25% research. The successful candidate is expected to establish an integrated Extension and applied research program addressing vegetable production across diverse production systems including commercial-scale production, small-acreage farming, market gardening, and community food systems. Program areas may include crop and cultivar selection, irrigation and fertility management, management of abiotic and biotic stresses, cover crops, and other emerging needs identified in collaboration with Oklahoma growers and industry stakeholders. Review of applications will begin on January 11, 2027 and will continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date will be on/after May 1, 2027. For more information about the Department of Horticulture and Landscape Architecture, please visit: https://agriculture.okstate.edu/departments-programs/hla/index.html . Oklahoma State University is a land-grant institution committed to excellence in diversity and inclusion. We strive to maintain a welcoming and inclusive environment that appreciates and values all members of the university community. More information concerning the OSU Office of Institutional Diversity can be found at: https://diversity.okstate.edu . Oklahoma State University strives to become the nation’s preeminent land-grant university. More information about the OSU Strategic Plan can be found at https://strategy.okstate.edu . Responsibilities: The successful candidate will work cooperatively with Extension educators, area and state specialists, growers, producers, farmers’ market organizations, and industry stakeholders to identify priority needs and develop, implement, and evaluate research-based Extension programs. The candidate will assess and continually improve the reach, effectiveness, and impact of these programs. The candidate will conduct applied research to evaluate and improve vegetable production practices and systems that are sustainable, economically viable, and socially responsible. The candidate will develop a high-impact, externally supported Extension and applied research program with statewide relevance and the potential for regional and national recognition. The candidate will disseminate program and research findings through peer-reviewed journal articles, Extension publications, grower handbooks, trade or industry publications, presentations, demonstrations, and other appropriate communication channels. Extension information will be shared through in-person programs, publications, field demonstrations, digital media, and other appropriate platforms. The candidate will participate actively in relevant professional societies and conferences and contribute to the broader professional community through collaboration and knowledge exchange. The candidate will develop and maintain effective grower and stakeholder relationships and travel throughout Oklahoma to conduct site visits, engage with growers and industry partners, provide research-based support and recommendations, and identify emerging needs and opportunities. Success in this position requires strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to build collaborative partnerships and establish trust with Extension colleagues, growers, producers, and other industry stakeholders. The candidate will conduct Extension programming and applied field research at one or more locations. Potential locations include the OSU Student Farm and The Botanic Garden at OSU in Stillwater, the OSU Cimarron Valley Research Station in Perkins, the OSU Mingo Valley Research Station in Bixby, and cooperating farms throughout Oklahoma. The candidate will recruit and mentor graduate students and serve as a major advisor and chair of graduate advisory committees in the Horticulture M.S. program and, as appropriate, the Crop Science, Food Science, or Environmental Science interdisciplinary Ph.D. programs. The candidate will contribute to graduate education through service on graduate advisory committees, work cooperatively with OSU faculty and staff, and serve as a member of the OSU vegetable crop production systems team. The candidate will provide appropriate service to the department, division, university, and profession; participate in relevant professional development activities; and complete required university, division, and departmental training. Qualifications: Required qualifications: An earned Ph.D. in Horticulture, Agronomy, Plant Sciences, Soil Science, Environmental Science, or a closely related field, with academic preparation or experience relevant to vegetable crop production. All degree requirements must be completed by the position start date. The successful candidate must demonstrate the ability to communicate effectively with professional and public audiences, travel throughout Oklahoma, and conduct Extension programming and applied field research. Preferred qualifications: Preferred qualifications include experience in Extension programming, applied research, or commercial production involving vegetable crops; evidence of scholarly and Extension productivity; experience developing competitive grant proposals or serving as a principal investigator or co-principal investigator on externally funded projects; experience assessing stakeholder needs and evaluating Extension program outcomes; demonstrated ability to communicate through in-person, written, digital, and multimedia formats; evidence of effective collaboration, leadership, and interpersonal skills; and the ability to lead multidisciplinary teams and contribute effectively as a team member. Salary: Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Application Procedures: Applications must be submitted online at: https://jobs.okstate.edu Applicants should submit: 1) a detailed letter of interest and fit for the position, 2) curriculum vitae, and 3) names and contact information for three professional references. All application materials should be submitted through the Oklahoma State University jobs website at: https://jobs.okstate.edu . Review of applications will begin after January 11, 2027, and will continue until the position is filled. Inquiries concerning this position may be sent to the position search and screening committee chair, Dr. Mike Schnelle, at mike.schnelle@okstate.edu. To learn more about OSU Agriculture and Stillwater, visit these websites. https://agriculture.okstate.edu https://agresearch.okstate.edu https://extension.okstate.edu https://www.okstate.edu https://www.visitstillwater.org https://www.stillwaterchamber.org All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 2d1348be Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) c960c367 Last Name (required) 9cf606a9 Email (required) 3493cb8b Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 0b49abbe Last Name (required) 7711da93 Email (required) de988341 Save this job for later c8f3b6b9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Postdoctoral Scholar BF9457 Stillwater DIV AGRICULTRL SCI & NATURAL RESRCS (STW) Visiting Research Scientist – Plant/ Crop Scientist-2179 Langston VP ACADEMIC AFFAIRS (LU) Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service BF9949 Stillwater DIV AGRICULTRL SCI & NATURAL RESRCS (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) 15cc6172 Last Name (required) 9298b3ff Email (required) 8fefe93f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies: These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Please choose a minimum education level"
