    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-af7746-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states-payne-county": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor AF7746 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States",
      "description": "Assistant Professor AF7746 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States - Payne County, Oklahoma, United States Assistant Professor AF7746 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States - Payne County, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor AF7746 Apply Now Assistant Professor AF7746 495280 Payne County Stillwater SPEARS SCHOOL OF BUSINESS (STW) Faculty Master's degree Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email David Carter david.carter@okstate.edu About this Position ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF FINANCE/REAL ESTATE The Department of Finance within the Spears School of Business at Oklahoma State University (OSU) invites applications for a tenure-track Faculty Position in Real Estate at the Assistant Professor level. The position is scheduled to start in August 2027. We are seeking candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our Real Estate and Property Management program. We expect that the individual in this position will foster effective, civil, and respectful working relationships with the Oklahoma State University campus community. JOB QUALIFICATIONS: We will consider candidates with Ph.Ds. in Real Estate or Finance with research and teaching experience in Real Estate. The successful candidate will have demonstrated the ability to add value to the department’s research mission by conducting high-quality Real Estate research, as well as educational programs through excellent teaching. The teaching load will consist of two Real Estate courses per semester at the undergraduate level. Potential courses could be Real Estate Finance, Real Estate Investment, and Real Estate Valuation. Teaching responsibilities are primarily in Stillwater but may occasionally be at the OSU-Tulsa campus. Candidates must possess an earned doctorate by August 1, 2027. Participation in service activities to the academic and business communities is expected and rewarded. We offer a competitive compensation package and excellent research support, including access to major finance databases and some specialized data sources, a minimum of 20 hours/week of graduate assistant support, and a research-active department with a terrific seminar series. TO APPLY: Applications will be accepted online at https://jobs.okstate.edu . The position number is #req 495280 and is found in the section labeled “Faculty”. Applicants should upload: 1) a letter of application, 2) a current curriculum vita, 3) evidence of teaching effectiveness, 4) a current working paper, and 5) contact information for three references. Any questions or inquiries should be directed to finance@okstate.edu . We will begin formally reviewing applications in October 2026, and we will continue to accept and review applications until the position is filled. Appropriate background checks (e.g. criminal background and credential checks) will be conducted. SALARY: Competitive and commensurate with experience and academic qualifications. The position is contingent upon available funding. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert f329d287 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Payne County, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Payne County, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level Master's degree Master's degree First Name (required) 122d69fe Last Name (required) 96fe2386 Email (required) d7e0f367 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) df8e07e3 Last Name (required) d4132cd7 Email (required) 6bcff564 Save this job for later e041442b Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Assistant Professor of Finance 213361 Payne County. Stillwater SPEARS SCHOOL OF BUSINESS (STW) Instructor 