    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/anatomic-pathology-resident-af7750-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Anatomic Pathology Resident AF7750",
      "description": "Anatomic Pathology Resident AF7750 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Anatomic Pathology Resident AF7750 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Anatomic Pathology Resident AF7750 Apply Now Anatomic Pathology Resident AF7750 495235 Stillwater COLLEGE OF VETERINARY MEDICINE (STW) Faculty Other professional degree Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Gayle Sisney, gayle.sisney@okstate.edu Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm with occasional evenings and weekends. Appointment Length Regular Continuous/Until Further Notice Hiring Range $50,000 Salary Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by 2026-10-31 to ensure full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume, cover letter, official transcripts from professional studies, TOEFL scores (if applicable) and at least three letters of references. About this Position The Department of Veterinary Pathobiology in the College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM) at Oklahoma State University (OSU) in beautiful Stillwater, OK, invites applications for our Anatomic Pathology Residency Training Position. We seek a motivated, hard-working, and dependable individual with a DVM or equivalent degree, a collegial attitude, and a keen interest in pursuing a career in anatomic pathology. Position Details: Full-Time Position: Annually renewed for up to 3 years Start Date: July 31, 2027 Salary: $50,000 per year plus a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance and fringe benefits. About the Program: Join a dynamic resident program with 3 anatomic pathology and 3 clinical pathology residents. Learn from 6 anatomic pathologists and 3 clinical pathologists on faculty with a wide range of expertise. Engage with extensive and varied diagnostic case material from the Oklahoma Animal Disease Diagnostic Laboratory (OADDL). Participate in rounds, seminars, and access abundant archived material for ACVP board preparation. Opportunities for creative scholarly activities and independent study. Benefits: Annual travel stipend of $1,500 for pathology courses, workshops, and meetings. One-time $500 stipend for books or other resource materials. Free access to Department of Wellness Facilities: https://wellness.okstate.edu/recreation/facilities/colvin.html Application Requirements: Current curriculum vitae Cover letter outlining career goals Official transcripts from professional studies TOEFL scores (if applicable) At least 3 letters of reference Application Deadline: For full consideration, applications should be received by October 31, 2026. How to Apply: Applicants can apply online at https://jobs.okstate.edu Inquiries: Please direct inquiries to Dr. Valerie McElliott, Residency Coordinator ( vmcelli@okstate.edu ). Note for International Candidates: Currently, our ability to sponsor candidates requiring work authorization for the U.S. is limited. Required Qualifications D.V.M. Veterinary Medicine (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity 