    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/open-rank-tenure-track-or-tenured-faculty-210551-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Tenure-Track or Tenured Faculty 210551",
      "description": "Open-Rank Tenure-Track or Tenured Faculty 210551 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Open-Rank Tenure-Track or Tenured Faculty 210551 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Open-Rank Tenure-Track or Tenured Faculty 210551 Apply Now Open-Rank Tenure-Track or Tenured Faculty 210551 495255 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Faculty PhD Open-Rank Tenure-Track or Tenured Faculty in Petroleum Engineering The Petroleum Engineering Program in the School of Chemical Engineering at Oklahoma State University seeks nominations and applications for an open-rank, tenure-track or tenured faculty position. Candidates shall have earned a doctorate in Petroleum Engineering or a closely related area and display a strong interest in undergraduate and graduate education. The successful applicant is expected to establish a nationally recognized, externally funded research program. Industrial experience is considered an asset. The primary areas of interest are drilling and completion engineering, but all candidates with a proven record of excellence in areas like production and hydraulic fracturing will also be considered. Oklahoma State University is making significant investments in energy education, research, and innovation. The College of Engineering, Architecture and Technology (CEAT), together with the Hamm Institute for American Energy, is building interdisciplinary capabilities to address the technological, economic, and workforce challenges facing the rapidly evolving energy industry. The successful candidate will have an opportunity to contribute to these initiatives while helping strengthen and expand Petroleum Engineering within the School of Chemical Engineering. We offer an undergraduate Minor in Petroleum Engineering designed to prepare students from across engineering disciplines for careers in the petroleum industry. We also offer M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in Petroleum Engineering, with graduate students working closely with faculty on a variety of research projects. The School currently includes approximately 16 faculty members, four of whom have a primary focus in Petroleum Engineering, and supports approximately 200 undergraduate and 50 graduate students across its programs. The School has a strong history of engagement with alumni and industry and benefits from substantial philanthropic and industrial support, including nine endowed chairs and professorships, faculty development endowments, and numerous research and educational partnerships. OSU's location provides exceptional access to the energy industry. Oklahoma and the surrounding region are home to major oil and gas operators, service companies, technology companies, and energy entrepreneurs, creating significant opportunities for collaborative research, technology development, student engagement, and industry-sponsored projects. The Petroleum Engineering program has historically benefited from strong relationships with both local and national energy companies. Qualifications: Candidates must have an earned Ph.D. in Petroleum Engineering or a closely related field by the anticipated start date. Preference will be given to a candidate with demonstrated expertise in drilling and completion engineering and who is also qualified to teach in areas such as petroleum production and stimulation. Applicants should demonstrate the potential to develop and sustain a nationally recognized, externally funded research program, a strong commitment to undergraduate and graduate education, and the ability to mentor graduate students effectively. Candidates should also possess strong communication and collaboration skills and be able to work effectively with academic colleagues and industry partners. Instructions to Applicants: Interested and qualified candidates should apply online at https://jobs.okstate.edu. A single pdf file is requested with your application. The file should include: cover letter; curriculum vitae; statement of teaching interests and philosophy; statement of research interests, including a plan to secure external funding with descriptions of two planned research projects; names and contact information of five professional references. Send requests for additional information to the search committee chair, Dr. Sundar Madihally, at chesearch@okstate.edu . Screening of applicants will begin as applications arrive and continue until the position is filled, contingent on available funding. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 3f572d45 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) 1e3d9769 Last Name (required) 5df9b37b Email (required) 9de9b0db Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) c98fc6e2 Last Name (required) cc717e62 Email (required) ce08de5e Save this job for later 08fb6598 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Open-Rank Tenure-track/Tenured Faculty 212552 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Assistant Professor 214515 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Assistant Professor 212507 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) cd91ddf8 Last Name (required) b5e88d81 Email (required) 5882d4d2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information