    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/open-rank-professor-of-computer-science-af9557-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor of Computer Science AF9557",
      "description": "Open Rank Professor of Computer Science AF9557 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Open Rank Professor of Computer Science AF9557 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Open Rank Professor of Computer Science AF9557 Apply Now Open Rank Professor of Computer Science AF9557 495237 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Faculty PhD Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Dr. Roger Mailler, faculty-search@cs.okstate.edu Work Schedule TBD Appointment Length 9 months or less Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by December 1, 2026, to ensure full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching philosophy, and contact information from a minimum of three professional references. For questions or more information, please contact faculty-search@cs.okstate.edu. About this Position Open Rank Professor of Computer Science The Oklahoma State University (OSU) Department of Computer Science is seeking applications for an open-rank tenure-track position with a start date of August 2027. Preferred research and teaching interests are in cybersecurity with an emphasis on digital forensics and cyber investigations , reverse engineering and malware analysis, and cybersecurity operations and incident management , or related areas with a solid track record in the core Computer Science domains. Responsibilities: Our department’s mission is to pursue and to publicize research projects in computer science in order to extend the present state of knowledge in the computer field, educate students in all program levels in order to provide them with the knowledge, interest, and ethics to become productive members of the computing profession, and serve as an initial and continuing source of education in the field of computer science. The successful candidate will demonstrate their alignment with this mission through a c lear research record along with the potential for teaching, support of program growth, and commitment to excellence in service and extension. Faculty are expected to pursue research collaborations with other faculty, industry, and research institutions as well as to further the university’s land grant mission through excellence in teaching and outreach activities. All faculty members are also expected to support the department's efforts in developing and teaching courses for o ur online certificate and degree programs and may be assigned to either the Tulsa or Stillwater campus. Junior faculty members are expected to be heavily research focused and during their first three years are only required to teach one course per semester. About the Department of Computer Science The OSU Department of Computer Science ( https://cs.okstate.edu ) is strongly committed to excellence in research, teaching, and outreach. The Department offers B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degrees in Computer Science, a B.S. degree in Applied Computer Programming, and two new interdisciplinary M.S. programs in Artificial Intelligence and Data Science. The Department also offers online courses to students at remote sites. Our recent student enrollment is approximately 420 undergraduate and 100 graduate students across all our majors with expected continued growth over the coming years. About Oklahoma State University Oklahoma State University is a Carnegie R1 research institution with a 130-year legacy as one of the nation’s model land-grant universities. Its beautiful Stillwater campus serves as the flagship of the OSU system, which enrolls more than 34,000 students. The College of Arts and Sciences offers exceptional strengths across the natural sciences, social sciences, and arts and humanities, complemented by institutional excellence in engineering, agriculture, and business. Together, these strengths support a collaborative intellectual environment and OSU’s longstanding commitment to research, teaching, and public engagement. Home to approximately 50,000 residents, Stillwater offers the welcoming atmosphere and affordability of a college town within an hour’s drive of two major metropolitan areas, Tulsa and Oklahoma City. The city benefits from a vibrant, university-centered intellectual and cultural community, with lectures, performances, exhibitions, Cowboy athletics, and traditions such as OSU’s signature Homecoming and Walkaround traditions. The McKnight Center for the Performing Arts brings internationally renowned artists and ensembles, including the New York Philharmonic, to Stillwater, while the OSU Botanic Garden, Block 34 park and amphitheater, Main Street, locally owned restaurants and breweries, parks, trails, and abundant outdoor recreation contribute to the city’s quality of life. Stillwater Regional Airport’s new passenger terminal and multiple daily flights to Dallas–Fort Worth provide convenient connections to destinations across the world. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Computer Science or closely related discipline (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date). Demonstrated research background as evidenced by conference and journal publications in high-quality venues commensurate with rank. Demonstrated ability to effectively mentor and collaborate with students and colleagues. Evidence of university-level teaching success commensurate with rank. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of successful grantsmanship. Evidence of the ability to create and/or manage a successful research or teaching program. Demonstrated knowledge and experience in program accreditation, which may include ABET or NSA NCAE. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 73ee2eee Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) 230e3157 Last Name (required) 98186217 Email (required) 82b1c960 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 1b8384fe Last Name (required) 20a53102 Email (required) 420693fb Save this job for later 5f82ff6c Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Open-Rank Tenure-track/Tenured Faculty 212552 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Assistant Professor (Management Science & Information Systems) 210018 Stillwater SPEARS SCHOOL OF BUSINESS (STW) Assistant Professor 214515 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) 5fc2b86f Last Name (required) bc4dc869 Email (required) 4654a212 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies: These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Please choose a minimum education level"
