    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-212507-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor 212507",
      "description": "Assistant Professor 212507 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Assistant Professor 212507 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor 212507 Apply Now Assistant Professor 212507 495204 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Faculty Master's degree Assistant Professor of Architecture, Tenure-Track The Oklahoma State University School of Architecture is accepting applications for a new nine-month, full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor faculty position in Architecture. The successful candidate will be required to teach architectural design studios as well as lecture and seminar courses in areas related to architecture. While the position is primarily focused on teaching, all faculty are expected to maintain a robust creative and scholarly agenda and engage in service activities that advance the mission and goals of the School, College, and University. Candidates with significant professional experience are strongly encouraged to apply. The ideal candidate will be versatile, capable of teaching both foundation and advanced-level design studios, will demonstrate a clear creative and scholarly agenda, and needs to have a second teaching emphasis, which could include but is not limited to Beginning Design, Graphic Communication, Theory and Criticism, Emerging Technologies, Building Systems, Materials, Professional Practice, or other relevant specialties. About the OSU School of Architecture Since 1909, the School of Architecture has provided professional education in architecture and architectural engineering, combining a rigorous design curriculum with a strong emphasis on the integration of technical and theoretical considerations within an enhanced academic environment. As a land-grant university, OSU embraces a mission of education, research, and service to advance the state and broader community. The school offers three undergraduate degree programs and a Graduate Certificate, supported by a dedicated faculty of 22, collaborating with a growing student body of 550 students. Degree programs offered through the School of Architecture include: Bachelor of Architecture: NAAB-accredited professional degree Bachelor of Architectural Engineering: ABET-accredited professional degree Bachelor of Science in Architectural Design Studies: Non-accredited degree Graduate Certificate in Integrative Design The School of Architecture fosters a collegial atmosphere among faculty, particularly through team-taught design studios. Collaborative and interdisciplinary scholarship is encouraged through the school’s integration of architecture and architectural engineering programs and is further supported by the school’s position within the College of Engineering, Architecture and Technology. State-of-the-art facilities advance the teaching and scholarship of both faculty and students. For more information about the school, faculty, and degree programs, please visit: https://ceat.okstate.edu/arch/ Candidate Credentials Candidates are required to hold a terminal degree through one of the following pathways: NAAB-accredited Bachelor of Architecture (B. Arch.) and post-professional degree (M. Arch. or master’s degree in a related field) and professional license NAAB-accredited Master of Architecture (M. Arch.) and professional license Ph.D. in Architecture or related field Applicants without a professional license (except those with a Ph.D.) may apply and receive full consideration for the position, but they will be required to outline a plan to achieve licensure prior to tenure review. Required Application Materials Interested applicants should apply online at https://jobs.okstate.edu. Candidates are required to upload the following documents via electronic PDF files: Letter of Interest, clearly outlining your qualifications and your areas of teaching and scholarship Curriculum Vitae (5-page limit) Statement of Teaching Philosophy (1-page limit) Statement of Scholarship/Research Agenda (1-page limit) Examples of Creative Professional Work, Academic Instruction emphasizing student work examples, and/or Scholarship (20-page limit) Three references, including contact information In addition to the online application, please send the documents listed above in a single PDF file to Professor John Phillips at john.j.phillips@okstate.edu . Total file size is not to exceed 20 MB. Timeline Review of applications will begin in November 2026 and continue until the position is filled. The successful candidate is expected to begin the faculty appointment in August 2027. Questions may be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee: Professor John Phillips ( john.j.phillips@okstate.edu ). All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 90023db7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level Master's degree Master's degree First Name (required) 764641a5 Last Name (required) ad9443aa Email (required) 0753ab1f Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 7a22d3a2 Last Name (required) c23f31f2 Email (required) fc28cd5e Save this job for later a1c2b0d8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Open-Rank Tenure-track/Tenured Faculty 212552 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Assistant Professor 214515 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Open-Rank Tenure-Track or Tenured Faculty 210551 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) 8cbfa468 Last Name (required) 5345bd89 Email (required) ce516398 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text 