    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/post-doctoral-fellow-af7761-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Fellow AF7761",
      "description": "Post Doctoral Fellow AF7761 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Post Doctoral Fellow AF7761 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Post Doctoral Fellow AF7761 Apply Now Post Doctoral Fellow AF7761 495148 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Adjunct/Temp Faculty PhD Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Dr. Sangita Sinha, sangita.sinha@okstate.edu Work Schedule TBD Appointment Length 12 months or less Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Special Instructions to Applicants Application Instructions: Candidates should submit the following: - Cover letter (including research interests and alignment with advertised position requirements) - Curriculum Vitae - Names and contact information for three references Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. About this Position Postdoctoral Fellow – College of Arts and Sciences, Oklahoma State University, Stillwater, Oklahoma The College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma State University invites applications for a Postdoctoral Fellow position within Prof. Sangita Sinha’s laboratory in the Microbiology and Molecular Genetics Department. This is a full-time, 12-month appointment with the possibility of renewal based on performance, funding availability, and college needs. The position is available immediately and will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. The College seeks to recruit dynamic, innovative scholars who are committed to excellence in research, scholarship, and academic collaboration. OSU’s College of Arts and Sciences is home to 23 departments across the humanities, social sciences, mathematics, and natural sciences, offering vibrant opportunities for interdisciplinary engagement. A bout OSU and the College of Arts and Sciences: Oklahoma State University is a Carnegie Tier 1 research institution with a 130-year legacy as one of the nation's premier land-grant universities. The Stillwater campus serves as the flagship of the OSU system which serves over 34,000 students and offers state-of-the-art facilities for research and instruction. The College of Arts and Sciences boasts exceptional strengths across the sciences, social sciences, arts and humanities, complemented by institutional excellence in engineering, agriculture, and business. Position Summary: The ideal candidate will have a strong background in protein structure and function characterization and be experienced in using a diverse range of biochemical, structural and molecular biology techniques to characterize proteins and protein interactions. The current focus of the Sinha lab is to develop a structure-based understanding of how cellular autophagy is regulated, and how autophagy is dysregulated in infectious diseases, cancers, neurodegenerative diseases, and cardiac myopathies. The candidate will also have the opportunity to contribute to new collaborative structural biology research projects. The candidate is also expected to assist the PI in writing research proposals and provide mentorship to undergraduate and graduate students. The position offers opportunities for independent research development, manuscript preparation, and grant writing. Responsibilities: Conduct independent and collaborative structural biology research focused on autophagy proteins, host pathogen reactions, and uncharacterized microbial proteins as directed by the PI. Publish scholarly work in peer-reviewed journals or other appropriate outlets. Participate in group meetings, departmental seminars and present research at national and international conferences. Assist in mentoring and training graduate and undergraduate students. Contribute to the development of grant proposals and new research directions. Participate in professional development opportunities offered by the College. Appointment Details: Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fellows receive a competitive benefits package. Initial appointment for one year, with possible renewal for two more years pending satisfactory progress. Required Qualifications Ph.D. M.D. or equivalent or terminal degree in Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, Microbiology, or a closely related field, with emphasis in protein biochemistry and structural biology (awarded by time of appointment). Demonstrated experience in creation of protein expression vectors and the purification and the biochemical characterization of proteins and protein complexes. Evidence of research productivity appropriate to career stage. Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Strong analytical, organizational, and scientific communication skills. A commitment to rigorous, ethical, and reproducible research practices. Ability to work collaboratively and contribute to a collaborative academic community. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in structure determination (CryoEM, X-ray crystallography, or NMR spectroscopy) of macromolecules and their assemblies. Experience developing and reproducibly performing cellular assays. Evidence of strong communication and mentoring skills. Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Demonstrated commitment to interdisciplinary research. Interest in contributing to broader impacts, community engagement, or public scholarship. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 93c4af4b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research Research Employment Type Adjunct/Temp Faculty Adjunct/Temp Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) e8c4cced Last Name (required) c7d3bb2e Email (required) 5da4ec96 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) fc2c39b7 Last Name (required) 2e4d1e97 Email (required) 957d7e23 Save this job for later 12a2fe53 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Post Doctoral Fellow AF7752 Payne County. Stillwater SPEARS SCHOOL OF BUSINESS (STW) Postdoctoral Fellow AF7765 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Assistant Professor of Sociology 215282 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) 40eeffdf Last Name (required) b91c94b5 Email (required) 57e6b784 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies Performance Cookie