    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/post-doctoral-fellow-af7752-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states-payne-county": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Fellow AF7752 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States",
      "description": "Post Doctoral Fellow AF7752 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States - Payne County, Oklahoma, United States Post Doctoral Fellow AF7752 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States - Payne County, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Post Doctoral Fellow AF7752 Apply Now Post Doctoral Fellow AF7752 495198 Payne County Stillwater SPEARS SCHOOL OF BUSINESS (STW) Faculty PhD Campus OSU-Stillwater MANAGEMENT SCIENCE AND INFORMATION SYSTEMS DEPARTMENT CENTER FOR HEALTH SYSTEMS INNOVATION The Department of Management Science and Information Systems (MSIS) and the Center for Health Systems Innovation (CHSI) in the Spears School of Business at Oklahoma State University invite applications for a Postdoctoral Fellow position. The position offers a flexible start date, but no later than the beginning of Fall 2027. Based on Oklahoma State University’s main campus in Stillwater, the position will focus on health data analytics research within CHSI and work closely with faculty in the MSIS department. ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: OSU’s MSIS Department has a unique blend of faculty, students and staff, delivering innovative academic programs at the undergraduate, master’s and doctoral level, producing impactful and high-quality research, and providing outstanding service to the profession, the university, the college and to the community. The Department has a long tradition of research and instructional programs in the data sciences. Faculty have published some of the top-cited research papers in decision support systems and business intelligence/data analytics history and continue this publishing excellence today. With the mission of Transforming Rural and Native American Health , OSU CHSI focuses on applying healthcare analytics, information technology, AI, and other data-driven methods to reshape and reform rural healthcare delivery. CHSI leverages large-scale Oracle Health EHR data for healthcare analytics and AI development and its ROK-Net rural clinic network for the evaluation and deployment of innovative healthcare technologies in real-world settings. ABOUT THE POSITION: The successful applicant should be a creative and effective researcher capable of contributing to CHSI and MSIS research, publications, and grant development activities. The fellow will support the development and implementation of processes and protocols for managing and maintaining the Oracle Health Real-World Data; assist with data integration, analysis, and quality assurance for new and existing sources of health-related data; and collaborate with healthcare organizations and other partners working with CHSI on research and innovation initiatives. Required skills and qualifications include: Strong understanding of relational databases and Apache Spark; knowledge of NoSQL databases is a plus. Demonstrated proficiency in analytics programming languages, such as Python and R. Demonstrated experience with machine learning, deep learning, and large language models (LLMs). Applicants should hold a Ph.D. in a relevant field and have an ongoing record of scholarly publications. At least two years of experience in healthcare data analytics and reporting is preferred. Knowledge of the healthcare industry and healthcare delivery environment is also preferred. Finally, the applicant should have an innovative mindset and be willing to support and participate in MSIS and CHSI initiatives as needed. This is a one-year appointment which could be extended for up to two additional years. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and academic qualifications. Applicant screening will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. All positions are contingent upon available funding. To Apply: Applicants can apply at jobs.okstate.edu by searching for 495198. Applicants should upload a letter of application, a resume/vitae, contact information for three references, a statement of research interests, relevant teaching evaluations, and other documentation that demonstrates applicant potential for the position. For inquiries regarding the application process, contact MSIS@okstate.edu . All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 42c37bae Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Payne County, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Payne County, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) 07fd4903 Last Name (required) 00cdbe2c Email (required) e3ac0d7a Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to 