    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-af7757-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor AF7757",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor AF7757 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Assistant/Associate Professor AF7757 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate Professor AF7757 Apply Now Assistant/Associate Professor AF7757 495117 Stillwater LIBRARY (STW) Faculty Master's degree The Oklahoma State University Library invites applications for a Patent, Trademark, and Government Documents Librarian . This position will focus on leading the University’s Patent and Trademark Resource Center (PTRC) as well as the government documents unit, which is the Regional Federal Depository Library in Oklahoma. We desire someone who is creative, has a passion for learning and engagement, and is eager to drive their own projects, while working collaboratively toward the mission and goals of the unit, the Library, and the University. This is a tenure-track faculty position reporting to the Associate Dean for Distinctive Collections. Responsibilities : The successful candidate will provide administrative leadership for the government documents unit and the PTRC, serving as a resource for students, staff, and faculty as well as the broader Oklahoma public. The successful candidate will also serve as the lead for the state’s Regional Federal Depository Library collection and will provide guidance and assistance to selective libraries in Oklahoma. In addition, this position will have liaison duties for the departments of History and Political Science. This person will provide relevant reference services, library instruction, collection development, and outreach and will work to develop collaborations on and off campus. Along with their everyday responsibilities, they will identify and implement new initiatives, build networks and relationships, and look for opportunities to expand the reach of their unit. This position will collaborate with others both within and outside of the Library and the OSU community. Required Qualifications : a Master’s in Library and Information Science demonstrated collegiality the ability to foster a collaborative environment exceptional core competencies including communication and organization ability to meet university standards for tenure-track faculty in scholarship, creative activity, and service Desired Qualifications: previous experience with government documents and databases past work with patent and trademark searches experience providing reference and instruction in a library setting Candidates are encouraged to view Dean Sheila Johnson’s expectations for Library leaders: https://library.okstate.edu/about-the-library/dean-of-libraries/leadership-expectations . For general information about the Library, see https://library.okstate.edu/about/dean-of-libraries/ . Compensation Package You will be offered a competitive salary minimum $65,000 for 11 months and benefits package in an area that enjoys a low cost of living. The package will include a generous holiday schedule and leave accrual. You will be offered start-up funding for research or travel and have access to the Library’s grant writer and development team as well as a full communications team. Deadline : For full consideration please attach a curriculum vitae, cover letter and list of three professional references. Application review begins on October 16, 2026 and continues until the position is filled. For consideration of your application materials, apply through jobs.okstate.edu and search for 495117. Along with the listed qualifications, please indicate in your cover letter any other professional experiences, certifications, or accomplishments that you would bring to this position. Questions about the application process may be directed to Mary Larson, Associate Dean for Distinctive Collections, at mary.larson@okstate.edu or 405-744-6588. Candidates will be asked to deliver a presentation to faculty and staff. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert ead8c474 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level Master's degree Master's degree First Name (required) 97d76057 Last Name (required) c811c750 Email (required) c6553e40 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your informatio