    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-sociology-215282-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sociology 215282",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Sociology 215282 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Assistant Professor of Sociology 215282 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Sociology 215282 Apply Now Assistant Professor of Sociology 215282 495119 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Faculty PhD Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Dr. Kelley Sittner, kelley.sittner@okstate.edu Work Schedule TBD Appointment Length 9 months or less Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by October 15, 2026, to ensure full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, research statement, copies of 2-3 selected scholarly papers, evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., sample syllabi, teaching evaluations), and contact information from a minimum of three professional references. About this Position Assistant Professor of Sociology The Department of Sociology at Oklahoma State University seeks applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Sociology with a start date of August 2027. Research and teaching interests should be in the criminology/criminal justice area. Responsibilities: The successful candidate will play a significant role in both the graduate and undergraduate teaching programs and will have a teaching load of two courses per semester. Courses taught at the undergraduate level may include but are not limited to Introduction to Criminal Justice, Sociology of Drugs, Comparative Perspectives of Criminal Justice Systems, and Juvenile Delinquency. Responsibilities also include participating in the mentoring of students and engagement in service activities as suitable for an assistant professor, such as participation on department and college-level committees, reviewing journal manuscripts, and other service to the profession. About the Department of Sociology Located within the College of Arts and Sciences, the Department of Sociology is recognized nationally for its excellence in research and commitment to undergraduate and graduate education. This distinction derives from a strong grounding in theoretical inquiry, creative promotion of critical thinking, and attention to diverse intellectual perspectives. The Department of Sociology offers Doctorate, Master’s and Bachelor’s degrees. About Oklahoma State University Oklahoma State University is a Carnegie R1 research institution with a 130-year legacy as one of the nation’s model land-grant universities. Its beautiful Stillwater campus serves as the flagship of the OSU system, which enrolls more than 34,000 students. The College of Arts and Sciences offers exceptional strengths across the natural sciences, social sciences, and arts and humanities, complemented by institutional excellence in engineering, agriculture, and business. Together, these strengths support a collaborative intellectual environment and OSU’s longstanding commitment to research, teaching, and public engagement. Home to approximately 50,000 residents, Stillwater offers the welcoming atmosphere and affordability of a college town within an hour’s drive of two major metropolitan areas, Tulsa and Oklahoma City. The city benefits from a vibrant, university-centered intellectual and cultural community, with lectures, performances, exhibitions, Cowboy athletics, and traditions such as OSU’s signature Homecoming and Walkaround events. The McKnight Center for the Performing Arts brings internationally renowned artists and ensembles, including the New York Philharmonic, to Stillwater, while the OSU Botanic Garden, Block 34 park and amphitheater, Main Street, locally owned restaurants and breweries, parks, trails, and abundant outdoor recreation contribute to the city’s quality of life. Stillwater Regional Airport’s new passenger terminal and multiple daily flights to Dallas–Fort Worth provide convenient connections to destinations across the world. Required Qualifications PhD in Sociology, Criminology or Criminal Justice by the time of the appointment. Demonstrated ability to teach at the college level, as evidenced by prior teaching experience, teaching philosophy, sample syllabi, or instructional training. Evidence of a robust research agenda with publications, or the potential to develop a strong record of scholarship, related to criminology and criminal justice. Preferred Qualifications Research interests in at least one of the department’s other specialty areas (collective behavior and social movements, environmental sociology, inequality, or social psychology). Experience securing, or working to obtain, external research funding. Evidence of successful college or university-level teaching and mentorship. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert a63ab1dd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) 6303f2be Last Name (required) 3408b314 Email (required) 68cced33 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 55d86abf Last Name (required) 069aa481 Email (required) 87ef865c Save this job for later bc2ae615 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Assistant Professor of Psychology AF7760 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Academic Advisor I - Sr Academic Advisor JS9928 Tulsa TULSA (TUL) Program Coordinator AS6368 Tulsa EDUCATION & HUMAN SCIENCES (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) 8111dca1 Last Name (required) 918d55d1 Email (requir