    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/open-rank-tenured-tenure-track-professor-of-clinical-psychology-af7754-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Open Rank Tenured/Tenure-Track Professor of Clinical Psychology AF7754",
      "description": "Open Rank Tenured/Tenure-Track Professor of Clinical Psychology AF7754 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Open Rank Tenured/Tenure-Track Professor of Clinical Psychology AF7754 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Open Rank Tenured/Tenure-Track Professor of Clinical Psychology AF7754 Apply Now Open Rank Tenured/Tenure-Track Professor of Clinical Psychology AF7754 495134 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Faculty PhD Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Dr. Stephanie Sweatt, stephanie.sweatt@okstate.edu Work Schedule TBD Appointment Length 9 months or less Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by October 15, 2026, to ensure full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, and contact information from a minimum of three professional references. About this Position Open Rank Professor of Clinical Psychology The Department of Psychology at Oklahoma State University invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured Professor of Clinical Psychology at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor, with a start date of August 2027. We are open to candidates in any area of clinical psychology but are particularly interested in candidates with specialties in Clinical Child Psychology, Pediatric Psychology, and Behavioral Medicine/Health Psychology. Responsibilities: Candidates are expected to have a strong background in and dedication to scholarly activity, excellent teaching and mentoring, and collegial engagement with faculty, staff, and students. They must also demonstrate the capacity to maintain a high-quality research program leading to scholarly productivity in the form of professional publications, presentations, and grantsmanship. Candidates will be expected to serve as research mentors for doctoral students, supervise undergraduate research, provide high-quality classroom instruction in both graduate and undergraduate courses, participate in our APA- and PCSAS-accredited PhD program in Clinical Psychology, and provide service to the department, college, and university. About the Department of Psychology The Department of Psychology at Oklahoma State University is committed to research, teaching, and outreach. The Department currently houses 22 tenured/tenure-track and 11 career-track full-time faculty and offers undergraduate programs in Psychology and Graduate programs in Clinical and Experimental Psychology. The Clinical Program, continuously APA-accredited since 1971 and PCSAS-accredited since 2018, is based on a clinical science model of training, and has subspecialties in Clinical Child, Pediatric Psychology, Health/Behavioral Medicine, and Adult Psychopathology. The Department is also home to the Center for Pediatric Psychology ( https://cas.okstate.edu/psychology/center_for_pediatric_psychology ), reflecting OSU’s 30+year history of dedication to training clinical psychology graduate students wishing to specialize in the field of pediatric psychology. The Experimental Program has concentrations in Developmental, Comparative-Neurobiological, Cognitive, and Social-Personality Psychology. The Department oversees and supports a large student body of approximately 50 doctoral students and 1300 undergraduate majors. Several of our current faculty maintain active research and training collaborations at both the University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center in Oklahoma City and the OSU College of Medicine in Tulsa, offering rich opportunities for access to medical specialty populations and collaborations. Additionally, OSU Stillwater, OSU College of Medicine, and OSU Tulsa partnered to host the interdisciplinary OSU Brain Initiative ( https://tulsa.okstate.edu/brain-initiative ) in Tulsa, OK, where the most advanced MRI system in the state is located, OSU Biomedical Imaging Center at the Hardesty Center for Clinical Research and Neuroscience: https://osumedicine.com/location/biomedical-imaging-center/ . Several current faculty maintain active research and training collaborations at the Hardesty Center for Clinical Research and Neuroscience, offering opportunities for access to medical specialty populations and collaborations. For more information about our department, please see our website ( http://psychology.okstate.edu ). About Oklahoma State University Oklahoma State University is a Carnegie R1 research institution with a 130-year legacy as one of the nation’s model land-grant universities. Its beautiful Stillwater campus serves as the flagship of the OSU system, which enrolls more than 34,000 students. The College of Arts and Sciences offers exceptional strengths across the natural sciences, social sciences, and arts and humanities, complemented by institutional excellence in engineering, agriculture, and business. Together, these strengths support a collaborative intellectual environment and OSU’s longstanding commitment to research, teaching, and public engagement. Home to approximately 50,000 residents, Stillwater offers the welcoming atmosphere and affordability of a college town within an hour’s drive of two major metropolitan areas, Tulsa and Oklahoma City. The city benefits from a vibrant, university-centered intellectual and cultural community, with lectures, performances, exhibitions, Cowboy athletics, and traditions such as OSU’s signature Homecoming and Walkaround traditions. The McKnight Center for the Performing Arts brings internationally renowned artists and ensembles, including the New York Philharmonic, to Stillwater, while the OSU Botanic Garden, Block 34 park and amphitheater, Main Street, locally owned restaurants and breweries, parks, trails, and abundant outdoor recreation contribute to the city’s quality of life. Stillwater Regional Airport’s new passenger terminal and multiple daily flights to Dallas–Fort Worth provide convenient connections to destinations across the world. Required Qualifications PhD in Clinical Psychology from an APA- or PCSAS-accredited clinical psychology program (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date). Completion of an APA-approved (or equivalent) clinical psychology internship. Evidence of high-quality research with a trajectory of building a national profile. Evidence of ability to effectively mentor and collaborate with students and colleagues. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of successful college or university-level teaching and/or mentorship. Certifications, Registrations, and/or Licenses: License eligible as a psychologist in Oklahoma. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Save this job for later First Name (required) 5c3aa185 Last Name (required) 70450b83 Email (required) 5c6f6eda Save this job for later f2516222 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Assistant Professor of Psychology AF7760 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Adjunct Professor - Psychology 900116 Oklahoma City OKLAHOMA CITY (OKC) Assistant Professor of Sociology 215282 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) a9fc410d Last Name (required) 636d58c2 Email (required) af1acd36 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessar