    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/open-rank-tenure-track-tenured-faculty-212552-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Tenure-track/Tenured Faculty 212552",
      "description": "Open-Rank Tenure-track/Tenured Faculty 212552 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Open-Rank Tenure-track/Tenured Faculty 212552 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Open-Rank Tenure-track/Tenured Faculty 212552 Apply Now Open-Rank Tenure-track/Tenured Faculty 212552 495102 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Faculty PhD Open-Rank Tenure-Track/Tenured Faculty Oklahoma State University (OSU) in Stillwater, Oklahoma, is inviting highly motivated and qualified candidates to apply for one open-rank tenure-track or tenured faculty position in the School of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE). The positions available can be filled at the assistant, associate, or full professor level, depending on the candidate's experience and qualifications. The focus areas are in Computer Engineering (encompassing computer architecture, machine learning, neural networks, embedded systems, software engineering, edge computing, cybersecurity, quantum computing, IoT, and VLSI design). Outstanding candidates in other areas of Electrical and Computer Engineering will also be considered on a case-by-case basis. The School of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) currently has 22 faculty members, approximately 460 undergraduate students, and 80 graduate students. ECE research advances intelligent, connected, and resilient engineering systems across AI, communications, sensing, computing, control, energy, and electronics. Major research strengths include AI, machine learning, and signal processing; robotics, autonomous systems, and intelligent control; wireless communications, RF/microwave, radar, and terahertz technologies; photonics, biomedical optics, and advanced sensing; power systems, renewable energy, smart grids, and resilient infrastructure; and microelectronics, semiconductor devices, embedded systems, and intelligent computing hardware. Across these research thrusts, AI, cybersecurity, advanced sensing, and cyber-physical systems provide strong interdisciplinary connections, enabling impactful applications in healthcare, aerospace, energy, transportation, defense, and next-generation communications. ECE faculty currently manage nearly $20 million in externally funded research grants, with annual research expenditures exceeding $2 million. The School of ECE offers B.S., M.S., M.Eng., and Ph.D. degrees in Electrical Engineering and a B.S. degree in Computer Engineering with an option in Software Engineering. ECE also participates in a new interdisciplinary M.S. in Artificial Intelligence program with multiple tracks, including Computer Science (CS), Computer Engineering (CpE), and Healthcare Administration (HCA). ECE’s baccalaureate programs are ABET accredited. Candidates must have an earned Ph.D. or equivalent in electrical engineering, computer engineering, computer science, or a closely related engineering field. Successful candidates will be expected to teach electrical and computer engineering courses; develop an externally funded, internationally recognized research program; demonstrate excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching; advise graduate students; and contribute service to ECE and the profession. Strong oral and written communication skills and the ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively are expected. Engineering experience in industry or government laboratories is desirable but not required. Candidates who can effectively utilize, share, leverage, and further develop existing ECE resources are particularly encouraged to apply. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 9a57a0ae Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) e1065db1 Last Name (required) 58c98ab5 Email (required) 34cb5a5c Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 2638e7f3 Last Name (required) af25df21 Email (required) f4e44523 Save this job for later ffdf9915 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Assistant Professor 214515 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Open Rank Professor of Computer Science AF9557 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Assistant Professor 212507 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) ee7000d7 Last Name (required) 233ce17b Email (required) 17029a20 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in res