    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-214515-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor 214515",
      "description": "Assistant Professor 214515 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Assistant Professor 214515 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor 214515 Apply Now Assistant Professor 214515 495103 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Faculty PhD Assistant Professor in the School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering The School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) at Oklahoma State University is pleased to invite applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position. Areas of emphasis for this position will include, but are not limited to, applied mechanics and mechanics of materials; machine learning, artificial intelligence, digital-twin modeling, biomechanics, and thermal system modeling; robotics, control, and unmanned/autonomous systems; advanced manufacturing; aerospace materials, structures, propulsion and power, and aerospace sustainment. The candidate will be expected to build an internationally recognized, externally funded research program and to contribute strongly to undergraduate and graduate teaching, student mentoring, and professional service. Candidates with research interests aligned with one of the centers, including CIBS (Center for Integrated Building Systems), OAIRE (Oklahoma Aerospace Institute for Research and Education), and LaunchPad Center for Advanced Mobility, are especially encouraged to apply. The School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering at Oklahoma State University has a strong local, national, and international reputation for its premier undergraduate and graduate education and research programs. As one of the largest academic units at Oklahoma State University, the school is home to over 1600 students, comprising over 1400 undergraduate students and 150 graduate students. The school has a total of 41 faculty members consisting of a vibrant combination of senior faculty and a large number of junior and motivated tenure-track members: 23 tenured, 11 tenure-track, and 7 teaching professors. Undergraduate laboratories are supported by more than 100000 sq.ft. of floor space in the ENDEAVOR building and the Design Manufacturing Laboratories. MAE offers undergraduate and graduate degrees on both the main campus and the Tulsa campus, reaching a varied population of traditional and non-traditional students. The School offers ABET-accredited degrees in both Mechanical Engineering and Aerospace Engineering. It also offers Master's and PhD degrees in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering, including an option for Unmanned Aerial Systems. The School is a unique blend of teaching and research excellence. Annual research expenditures are nearly $300K per tenured/tenure-track faculty member, and new external research awards received for FY26 average $350K per tenured/tenure-track faculty member. The school is home to several national and statewide programs, including CIBS (Center for Integrated Building Systems), OAIRE (Oklahoma Aerospace Institute), NASA Oklahoma Space Grant EPSCoR, and the LaunchPad Center for Advanced Mobility. Research is supported across multiple large-scale facilities including the Advanced Technology Research Center, EXCELSIOR, the Helmerich Research Center (Tulsa), and the dedicated 80-acre Unmanned Systems Flight Station. The School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering is one of the nine schools within the College of Engineering, Architecture and Technology, which encompasses both the Stillwater and Tulsa campuses and has about 3800 undergraduate students, 700 graduate students, and 170 full-time faculty. Oklahoma State University is an R1, comprehensive land-grant university with over 27000 students. Stillwater is a safe city of 50000 residents with strong public schools and affordable, high-quality housing. Travel is convenient with a brand-new airport in Stillwater, as well as flight options from two cosmopolitan cities, Tulsa and Oklahoma City, which are only 65 miles away. Qualifications: An earned Ph.D. in a field closely aligned with mechanical or aerospace engineering is required. Successful candidates should have research expertise in a rapidly developing area in mechanical or aerospace engineering fields with strong potential for securing competitive extramural funding, essential for building an internationally recognized research program. Applications: Interested and qualified candidates should apply online at https://jobs.okstate.edu. A single PDF file is requested with your application. The file should include: a cover letter, a detailed curriculum vitae, a statement of research, including descriptions of two planned research projects, a statement of teaching interests and vision, names and contact information of five professional references. Send requests for additional information to the search committee chair, Dr. Mike Xiang at yujiang.xiang@okstate.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received by December 1, 2026, will receive full consideration. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert d826d561 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) 7b4ca335 Last Name (required) 928072a0 Email (required) 40d61b81 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 2d5b9f18 Last Name (required) 1dca4a58 Email (required) e2493dbb Save this job for later fc094b42 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Open-Rank Tenure-track/Tenured Faculty 212552 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Assistant Professor 212507 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Open Rank Professor of Computer Science AF9557 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) 29f7a240 Last Name (required) bca68e7a Email (required) ade55bda Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies: These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move aroun