    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-psychology-af7760-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology AF7760",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Psychology AF7760 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Assistant Professor of Psychology AF7760 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Psychology AF7760 Apply Now Assistant Professor of Psychology AF7760 495127 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Faculty PhD Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Dr. Shelia Kennison, shelia.kennison@okstate.edu Work Schedule TBD Appointment Length 9 months or less Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by October 15, 2026, to ensure full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, and contact information from a minimum of three professional references. About this Position Assistant Professor of Psychology The Department of Psychology at Oklahoma State University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Psychology with an anticipated start date of August 2027. We seek a scholar with a program of high-quality research in neuroscience, neurobiology, biological basis of behavior, or a closely related area who can teach courses in neurobiological bases of behavior at the graduate and undergraduate levels. Area of specialization is open, and we welcome candidates from cognitive, social, developmental, health, clinical or related areas. Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain a competitive and productive program of high-quality research, leading to scholarly professional publications, presentations, and grantsmanship. Candidates should be strongly committed to excellence in both research and teaching. The candidate will also be expected to teach courses in Neurobiological Psychology at graduate and undergraduate levels and provide research training and mentorship for doctoral and undergraduate students. Responsibilities will also include service to the department, college, and university. About the Department of Psychology The Department of Psychology at Oklahoma State University is committed to research, teaching, and outreach. The Department currently houses 22 tenured/tenure-track and 11 career-track full-time faculty and offers undergraduate programs in Psychology and Graduate programs in Experimental and Clinical Psychology. The Experimental Program has concentrations in Developmental, Comparative-Neurobiological, Cognitive, and Social-Personality Psychology and is home to the Oklahoma Center for Evolutionary Analysis (OCEAN). The Clinical Program, continuously APA-accredited since 1971 and PCSAS-accredited since 2018, is based on a clinical science model of training, and has subspecialties in Clinical Child, Pediatric Psychology, Health/Behavioral Medicine, and Adult Psychopathology. The Department is also home to the Center for Pediatric Psychology ( https://cas.okstate.edu/psychology/center_for_pediatric_psychology ), reflecting OSU’s 30+year history of dedication to training clinical psychology graduate students wishing to specialize in the field of pediatric psychology. The Department oversees and supports a large student body of approximately 50 doctoral students and 1300 undergraduate majors. Several of our current faculty maintain active research and training collaborations at both the University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center in Oklahoma City and the OSU College of Medicine in Tulsa, offering rich opportunities for access to medical specialty populations and collaborations. Additionally, OSU Stillwater, OSU College of Medicine, and OSU Tulsa partnered to host the interdisciplinary OSU Brain Initiative ( https://tulsa.okstate.edu/brain-initiative ) in Tulsa, OK, where the most advanced MRI system in the state is located, OSU Biomedical Imaging Center at the Hardesty Center for Clinical Research and Neuroscience: https://osumedicine.com/location/biomedical-imaging-center/ . Several current faculty maintain active research and training collaborations at the Hardesty Center for Clinical Research and Neuroscience, offering opportunities for access to medical specialty populations and collaborations. For more information about our department, please see our website ( http://psychology.okstate.edu ). About Oklahoma State University Oklahoma State University is a Carnegie R1 research institution with a 130-year legacy as one of the nation’s model land-grant universities. Its beautiful Stillwater campus serves as the flagship of the OSU system, which enrolls more than 34,000 students. The College of Arts and Sciences offers exceptional strengths across the natural sciences, social sciences, and arts and humanities, complemented by institutional excellence in engineering, agriculture, and business. Together, these strengths support a collaborative intellectual environment and OSU’s longstanding commitment to research, teaching, and public engagement. Home to approximately 50,000 residents, Stillwater offers the welcoming atmosphere and affordability of a college town within an hour’s drive of two major metropolitan areas, Tulsa and Oklahoma City. The city benefits from a vibrant, university-centered intellectual and cultural community, with lectures, performances, exhibitions, Cowboy athletics, and traditions such as OSU’s signature Homecoming and Walkaround traditions. The McKnight Center for the Performing Arts brings internationally renowned artists and ensembles, including the New York Philharmonic, to Stillwater, while the OSU Botanic Garden, Block 34 park and amphitheater, Main Street, locally owned restaurants and breweries, parks, trails, and abundant outdoor recreation contribute to the city’s quality of life. Stillwater Regional Airport’s new passenger terminal and multiple daily flights to Dallas–Fort Worth provide convenient connections to destinations across the world. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Psychology or closely related field (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date). Evidence of high-quality research with a trajectory of building a national profile. Evidence of successful college or university-level teaching and/or mentorship. Evidence of an ability to effectively mentor and collaborate with students. Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Specialization in cognitive, social, developmental, health, clinical or related areas. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert fcb7f3e5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) 9455bb79 Last Name (required) b084f526 Email (required) 8bea00a9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 222bbc8b Last Name (required) d26e5558 Email (required) d39db541 Save this job for later 167605ef Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Open Rank Tenured/Tenure-Track Professor of Clinical Psychology AF7754 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Assistant/Associate Professor 210218 Tulsa CENTER FOR HEALTH SCIENCES (CHS) Adjunct Professor - Psychology 900116 Oklahoma City OKLAHOMA CITY (OKC) Apply Now! First Name (required) b6017e56 Last Name (required) f6517f63 Email (required) 4a1c2566 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies: These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Please choose a minimum education level"
