    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-political-science-af7758-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science AF7758",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Political Science AF7758 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Assistant Professor of Political Science AF7758 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Political Science AF7758 Apply Now Assistant Professor of Political Science AF7758 495126 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Faculty PhD Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Dr. Peter Rudloff, peter.rudloff@okstate.edu Work Schedule TBD Appointment Length 9 months or less Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by October 15, 2026, to ensure full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy and research statements, evidence of successful teaching and research, and contact information from a minimum of three professional references. About this Position Assistant Professor of Political Science The Department of Political Science at Oklahoma State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Law and Politics starting August 2027. Responsibilities: Teaching responsibilities will be on a 2-2 load and consist of introductory, upper-level undergraduate courses, as well as graduate seminars offered either in person or online. The successful candidate will teach courses contributing to our Pre-Law option within the Political Science major and the Law and Legal Studies minor. We are also highly interested in candidates able to teach introduction to American Government. A Ph.D. in Political Science is required at the time of appointment. Candidates with a J.D. degree and a license to practice law in the United States are particularly encouraged to apply. About the Department of Political Science The Department of Political Science is housed within the College of Arts and Sciences and offers B.S. and B.A. degrees, with degree options in campaigning, global politics, pre-law, and public policy. It also offers M.A. degrees in Politics and Policy Studies, as well as Peace, Conflict, and Security Studies. About Oklahoma State University Oklahoma State University is a Carnegie R1 research institution with a 130-year legacy as one of the nation’s model land-grant universities. Its beautiful Stillwater campus serves as the flagship of the OSU system, which enrolls more than 34,000 students. The College of Arts and Sciences offers exceptional strengths across the natural sciences, social sciences, and arts and humanities, complemented by institutional excellence in engineering, agriculture, and business. Together, these strengths support a collaborative intellectual environment and OSU’s longstanding commitment to research, teaching, and public engagement. Home to approximately 50,000 residents, Stillwater offers the welcoming atmosphere and affordability of a college town within an hour’s drive of two major metropolitan areas, Tulsa and Oklahoma City. The city benefits from a vibrant, university-centered intellectual and cultural community, with lectures, performances, exhibitions, Cowboy athletics, and traditions such as OSU’s signature Homecoming and Walkaround traditions . The McKnight Center for the Performing Arts brings internationally renowned artists and ensembles, including the New York Philharmonic, to Stillwater, while the OSU Botanic Garden, Block 34 park and amphitheater, Main Street, locally owned restaurants and breweries, parks, trails, and abundant outdoor recreation contribute to the city’s quality of life. Stillwater Regional Airport’s new passenger terminal and multiple daily flights to Dallas–Fort Worth provide convenient connections to destinations across the world. Required Qualifications PhD in Political Science; candidates who are ABD will be expected to finish their degree requirements before the Fall 2027 semester. Evidence of high-quality research with a trajectory of building a national profile. Evidence of successful college or university-level teaching and mentorship. Demonstrated ability to effectively mentor and collaborate with students and colleagues. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert f7cb10d8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) 258cbb7f Last Name (required) 2115a194 Email (required) 7408e893 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 6925f922 Last Name (required) 147d98e7 Email (required) ca68de75 Save this job for later e1e34500 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Assistant Professor 214515 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Assistant / Associate Professor 212327 Stillwater SPEARS SCHOOL OF BUSINESS (STW) Assistant Professor of Sociology 215282 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) 4d220b76 Last Name (required) 1b9b5099 Email (required) 56ae12aa Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and t