    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-ad9443-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty AD9443",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty AD9443 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Adjunct Faculty AD9443 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty AD9443 Apply Now Adjunct Faculty AD9443 495104 Stillwater ENGINEERING, ARCHITECTR & TECHNOLGY (STW) Adjunct/Temp Faculty PhD Adjunct Faculty - Spring 2027 The School of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) at Oklahoma State University (OSU) invites applications for an adjunct instructor for Spring 2027. We seek a highly motivated and qualified candidate with teaching and/or research experience in the areas of power and energy systems . The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching a senior-level course ECEN 4173 Power System Operation and Intelligence . Applicants must hold an earned Ph.D. or equivalent degree in electrical engineering, computer engineering, or a closely related engineering field. Prior teaching experience in power and energy systems is preferred. The School of ECE offers B.S., M.S., M.Eng., and Ph.D. degrees in Electrical Engineering, as well as a B.S. degree in Computer Engineering with an option in Software Engineering. ECE also participates in a new interdisciplinary M.S. in Artificial Intelligence with multiple tracks, including Computer Science (CS), Computer Engineering (CpE), and Healthcare Administration (HCA). ECE’s baccalaureate programs are ABET accredited. Interested and qualified candidates should apply online at http://jobs.okstate.edu. Multiple PDF files are requested with your application: A cover letter; curriculum vitae. Send requests for additional information to Head of ECE, Dr. Guoliang Fan at guoliang.fan@okstate.edu . Recruitment will continue until the position is filled. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 392b8042 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Adjunct/Temp Faculty Adjunct/Temp Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) b5dccf13 Last Name (required) feadd178 Email (required) 2568fcb0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 89ccb507 Last Name (required