    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-fellow-af7765-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow AF7765",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Fellow AF7765 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Postdoctoral Fellow AF7765 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Fellow AF7765 Apply Now Postdoctoral Fellow AF7765 495060 Stillwater ARTS AND SCIENCES (STW) Faculty PhD Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Dr. Marianna Patrauchan, m.patrauchan@okstate.edu Work Schedule TBD Appointment Length 12 months or less Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Priority Application Date Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates should submit the following: - Cover letter (including research interests and alignment with advertised position requirements) - Curriculum Vitae - Names and contact information for three references About this Position The College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma State University invites applications for a Postdoctoral Fellow position in Dr. Patrauchan laboratory, Department of Microbiology and Molecular Genetics. This is a full-time, 12-month appointment with the possibility of annual renewal for two additional years based on performance, funding availability, and college needs. The College seeks to recruit dynamic, innovative scholars who are committed to excellence in research, scholarship, and academic collaboration. OSU’s College of Arts and Sciences is home to 23 departments across the humanities, social sciences, mathematics, and natural sciences, offering vibrant opportunities for interdisciplinary engagement. Responsibilities: Conduct independent and collaborative research to study the molecular mechanisms by which calcium signaling regulates cell differentiation and biomineralization during biofilm development and integrates with other signaling systems in the human pathogen Pseudomonas aeruginosa. Participate actively in laboratory meetings, departmental seminars, and collaborative research activities. Publish scholarly work in peer-reviewed journals. Assist with mentoring graduate and undergraduate students. Contribute to the development of grant proposals and new research directions. Required Qualifications A Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in Microbiology, Molecular Biology, Biochemistry or closely related discipline by the position’s start date (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date). Demonstrated research experience in bacterial physiology and genetics, molecular cloning, transcriptomics, and microscopy. Evidence of research productivity appropriate to career stage. Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Strong analytical, organizational, and scientific communication skills. A commitment to rigorous, ethical, and reproducible research practices. Preferred Qualifications Experience in recombinant protein work and biochemical characterization. Evidence of strong communication and mentoring skills. Appointment Details: Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fellows receive a competitive benefits package. Initial appointment for one year, with possible annual renewal for two additional years pending satisfactory progress. This position is contingent on the availability of funding. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 50412941 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research Research Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) 4171470e Last Name (required) c8413385 Email (required) 046d81c7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 0cf53d2f Last Name (required) 8c81a02e Email (required) 5e32b552 Save this job for later 87177d2b Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank