    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-212327-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate Professor 212327",
      "description": "Assistant / Associate Professor 212327 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Assistant / Associate Professor 212327 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant / Associate Professor 212327 Apply Now Assistant / Associate Professor 212327 495051 Stillwater SPEARS SCHOOL OF BUSINESS (STW) Faculty PhD Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Dr. Craig A. Sisneros. Craig.Sisneros@okstate.edu About this Position The School of Accounting (SOA) within the Spears School of Business (SSB) at the Oklahoma State University invites applications for one tenure track Faculty Position in Accounting at the level of Assistant or Associate Professor level starting August 2027 at our main campus in Stillwater. This position is benefits eligible. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and contingent on available funding. Appropriate background checks (e.g. criminal background and credential checks) will be conducted. JOB DESCRIPTION : All candidates must have and maintain qualifications for AACSB accreditation by conducting and publishing scholarly research, attending professional conferences and workshops, providing editorial service, etc. The primary responsibilities for this position include research, teaching, and engaging in service activities for the School of Accounting, the Spears School of Business, and the academic discipline. Audit-focused candidates are preferred as primary teaching responsibilities will be in Audit courses at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: An earned doctorate in accounting or strong evidence that the doctoral degree will be completed before August 1, 2027. Candidates must be able to teach successfully at the undergraduate and master’s levels. Candidates must be academically qualified upon the start date and must maintain qualifications. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Significant professional and/or teaching experience in Audit is desirable with evidence of successful teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level. For an experienced Assistant or Associate Professor, we are especially interested in candidates who have a publishing record in top academic accounting journals, who indicate an interest in and ability to work with PhD students, and who will continue to produce research of excellent quality that will have a high impact on the field. For an Assistant Professor, evidence of the ability to progress toward these goals is preferred. TO APPLY: Applicants should upload: 1) a letter of application, 2) a current curriculum vita, 3) evidence of teaching effectiveness, 4) a current working paper, and 5) names and contact information of three references (applicants will be notified before we contact references). Applications will continue to be accepted and reviewed until the position has been filled. Inquiries may be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Craig A. Sisneros. (Craig.Sisneros@okstate.edu) All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 03b54e97 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) b7664b80 Last Name (required) 8eb52f7b Email (required) b4d2d807 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) 58381227 Last Name (required) ac7bc007 Email (required) a360573b Save this job for later 7817478a Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Instructor of Professional Practice 22154 Payne County. Stillwater SPEARS SCHOOL OF BUSINESS (STW) Assistant Professor of Professional Practice AF8119 Payne County SPEARS SCHOOL OF BUSINESS (STW) Assistant/Associate Professor in 