    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/associate-vice-president-of-the-oklahoma-cooperative-extension-service-bf9949-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service BF9949",
      "description": "Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service BF9949 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service BF9949 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service BF9949 Apply Now Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service BF9949 494914 Stillwater DIV AGRICULTRL SCI & NATURAL RESRCS (STW) Faculty PhD Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Martin Baker, Martin@buffkinbaker.com Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm with occasional evenings and weekends. Appointment Length Regular Continuous/Until Further Notice Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for three professional references. Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by 2026-11-01 to ensure full consideration. About this Position The Division of Agricultural Sciences and Natural Resources (DASNR), Oklahoma State University, invites nominations and applications for the position of Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Cooperative Extension Service (OCES). This 12-month position is administratively responsible to the Vice President, Dean and Director, Division of Agricultural Sciences and Natural Resources. The OCES employs more than 400 faculty, professional, and support staff. Employees are located on the OSU campus and in more than 80 locations throughout Oklahoma. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to the land-grant mission. The OCES Associate Vice President is the chief operating officer of OCES and will provide transformative statewide, regional, and national leadership in fostering high-quality and effective Cooperative Extension Service programs relevant to Oklahoma needs. The incumbent will: • Lead long-range program planning, implementation and reporting for the OCES system. • Work with the DASNR Vice President, Dean and Director to administer programs, personnel, and fiscal affairs. • Provide leadership to increase revenue for OCES with county, state, federal, and private sources. • Provide leadership for engagement with county and state leaders and legislators to enhance extension programming. • Actively seek input on program needs and to garner support for OCES from food and agricultural organizations, natural resource organizations, community health and wellness organizations, and other stakeholders. • Help lead campus-wide initiatives on Extension and coordinate with the Associate Vice President, Oklahoma Agricultural Experiment Station (OSU Ag Research), Associate Dean of the Ferguson College of Agriculture (Academic Programs), the Deans and extension leads from other Colleges at Oklahoma State University including the Colleges or Education and Human Sciences, Engineering, Architecture and Technology, Spears School of Business, Veterinary Medicine, and Arts & Sciences to achieve effective coordination of Extension programs. • Manage day-to-day operations of OCES administrative issues. • Maintain an active role in regional and national organizations such as the Association of Southern Region Extension Directors and Association of Public and Land Grant Universities. • Actively engage with the USDA National Institute for Food and Agriculture, the Oklahoma Department of Agriculture, Food and Forestry, and other federal and state agencies to coordinate Extension and outreach efforts across organizations to position OCES for funding opportunities. • Provide leadership for full compliance with the Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Program in the OCES. • Serve as a member of DASNR’s executive team and coordinate with the Dean and VP, Associate Dean of the Ferguson College of Agriculture, and the Associate Vice President of the Oklahoma Agricultural Experiment Station to advance OSU Agriculture and ensure synergies with teaching, research, and Extension missions. Required Qualifications A terminal degree in a discipline related to the Cooperative Extension Service mission is preferred; exceptions may be made for individuals with exceptional leadership and administrative experience related to the OCES mission; (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) Experience leading a complex organization with multiple layers of direct reports is strongly preferred; A comprehensive understanding of non-formal youth and adult education and program development processes; A demonstrated ability to serve effectively as an administrative leader; a proven ability to communicate effectively; and a demonstrated capability to manage personnel and budgets; An understanding of issues important to Oklahoma agriculture, families, youth and communities and a grasp of the means to provide visionary and progressive leadership in the development of innovative programs; A thorough understanding of all levels, programming areas, and aspects of the Cooperative Extension Service is essential with the ability to strengthen relationships with constituency groups at the county, state, and federal level. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in the Cooperative Extension System is preferred. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 92f31d28 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Cooperative Extension Executive/Administrative/Managerial Cooperative Extension Executive/Administrative/Managerial Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) c7f4e220 Last Name (required) f00ea40d Email (required) 47c01e75 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) a9d19615 Last Name (required) b95014e2 Email (required) e032f414 Save this job for later 6ae29613 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Extension Learning and Development Program Director CS9612 Stillwater DIV AGRICULTRL SCI & NATURAL RESRCS (STW) Extension State Program Specialist CS9607 Stillwater DIV AGRICULTRL SCI & NATURAL RESRCS (STW) Manager of Grants Financial Reporting & Accounting AS6385 Stillwater ADMINISTRATION AND FINANCE (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) 8578d1e2 Last Name (required) fa5b5690 Email (required) fbab41f2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies, which may impact your user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. We will never sell your data to third parties. Review your institution's privacy policy below: OSU's privacy notice Langston University's privacy notice Northeastern Oklahoma A&M's privacy notice Connors State College privacy notice Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usu