    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-management-science-information-systems-210018-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Management Science & Information Systems) 210018",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Management Science & Information Systems) 210018 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Assistant Professor (Management Science & Information Systems) 210018 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor (Management Science & Information Systems) 210018 Apply Now Assistant Professor (Management Science & Information Systems) 210018 492818 Stillwater SPEARS SCHOOL OF BUSINESS (STW) Faculty PhD ASSISTANT PROFESSOR MANAGEMENT SCIENCE AND INFORMATION SYSTEMS DEPARTMENT OKLAHOMA STATE UNIVERSITY STILLWATER CAMPUS The Management Science and Information Systems (MSIS) Department in the Spears School of Business at Oklahoma State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position slated to begin in Fall 2027. The position is on the Stillwater campus. Departmental faculty, such as this position, are in both Stillwater and Tulsa and can teach classes in both locations (as well as on-line as appropriate). OSU’s MSIS Department has a unique blend of faculty, students and staff, delivering innovative academic programs at the undergraduate, master’s and doctoral level, producing impactful and high-quality research, and providing outstanding service to the profession, the university, the college and the community. The Department has a long tradition of research and instructional program excellence in MIS, Cybersecurity, and Data Science. The Department also partners with OSU’s Center for Health Sciences and the Center of Health Systems Innovation in delivering graduate programs and certificates, and conducting applied research, in health informatics and health care analytics. The Department remains a national leader in Information Assurance (IA), having been previously designated a National Center of Academic Excellence in IA Education (CAE/IAE) and Research (CAE-R) by the NSA and the Department of Homeland Security and maintaining its status as an Education Partner with the NSA and its STEM programs. Degree programs administered in the department include the BSBA in MIS, with options in Data Science, as well as Information Assurance, a BSBA in Data Analytics, a Masters in MIS, a thriving doctoral program, and several certificate programs including Supply Chain Management (in conjunction with the School of Marketing). Three large enrollment core business classes in the Spears School are taught by MSIS faculty. Faculty also support the MBA program, the M.S. in Accounting programs, and the interdisciplinary college level M.S. in Business Analytics and Data Science program. While applicants with all areas of MIS expertise are welcomed, preference will be given to candidates who can teach large, business core classes in information systems and/or data science, and those with a strong background in cybersecurity. Technical versatility is a plus. The preferred applicant should be engaged in impactful research with aspirations of publishing in top journals in MIS, Data Science and/or Cybersecurity. Finally, applicants should have an innovative mindset and be willing to support and participate in departmental initiatives as needed. To be considered for the position, the preferred applicant will have completed a Ph.D. in MIS or related area from an AACSB-accredited university. Those close to finishing their degree (e.g., ABD status) will also be considered. Applicant screening will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. The position is contingent upon available funding. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and academic qualifications. The appointment is a tenure-track position and the normal personnel process of the SSB and OSU applies. To Apply: Applicants can apply at jobs.okstate.edu by searching for 492818. Applicants should upload a letter of application, a resume/vitae, contact information for three references, a statement of research interests, relevant teaching evaluations, and other documentation that demonstrates applicant potential for the position. For inquiries regarding the application process, contact MSIS@okstate.edu . All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 7e365a9b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) 0c37eca9 Last Name (required) 4ba0a041 Email (required) 30cb2e04 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within 