    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/clinical-skills-teaching-assistant-associate-professor-af8114-stillwater-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Skills Teaching Assistant/Associate Professor AF8114",
      "description": "Clinical Skills Teaching Assistant/Associate Professor AF8114 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Clinical Skills Teaching Assistant/Associate Professor AF8114 - Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Clinical Skills Teaching Assistant/Associate Professor AF8114 Apply Now Clinical Skills Teaching Assistant/Associate Professor AF8114 494388 Stillwater COLLEGE OF VETERINARY MEDICINE (STW) Faculty Other professional degree Campus OSU-Stillwater Contact Name & Email Allison Biddick, allison.biddick@okstate.edu Work Schedule TBD Appointment Length 11 months Hiring Range Commensurate with experience Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration please include a cover letter, resume and contact information for three professional references with application. About this Position The Oklahoma State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a teaching track position at the rank of assistant professor in the Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences to join a Clinical Skills Teaching team comprised of three other DVM faculty practitioners, a Program Director, and a Program Manager (RVT). We are seeking an enthusiastic small animal or mixed animal veterinarian with a passion for teaching to join this team. The successful applicant will be an integral part of the instructional team in years 1-3 of the DVM professional program. Position is contingent upon available funding. Teaching responsibilities will include didactic and clinical instruction, focusing on small animal clinical skills as well as clinical reasoning and communication. The successful applicant will be a full-time educator with most effort devoted to teaching in the clinical skills program, however, applicants are encouraged to devote up to 25% effort in clinical service and instruction of small animal emergency and critical care in the Veterinary Teaching Hospital. Collaboration on scholarly activities such as research and publications is optional based on the interests of the successful candidates. The Dr. Donald Holmes Clinical Skills Lab is a 2,200 square feet state-of-the-art education and assessment resource featuring a large open lab with flexible workspaces and over 1,000 additional square feet of devoted storage and model workshop areas. High quality audiovisual and lecture capture technology and projectors are included in these spaces for enhanced learning opportunities. New, updated communication pods for high quality experiential learning were completed earlier this year. High and low fidelity models and simulators are available for both small and large animal skills. Additional teaching spaces and facilities are available for skills instruction, including live animal skills. This position will serve a critical role in contributing to the CVM mission of being a world leader in veterinary professional education. Stillwater is a great place to live and was named one of the best small towns in America and the best college town in Oklahoma. It has a population of 50,000, located in central Oklahoma, approximately 60 miles from Tulsa and Oklahoma City. Numerous activities are available including camping, hiking, golf courses, state parks, lakes for boating and fishing, theatre productions including the newly opened McKnight Center located on the OSU campus, rodeos, the excitement of Big XII sporting events and more. For more information on Stillwater, you can visit www.stillwaterchamber.org . Review of applicants will begin upon receipt of applications and will continue until the position is filled. Application including letter of intent, curriculum vitae, and three names of references with contact information should be submitted at jobs.okstate.edu. For inquiries please contact: Dr. Allison Biddick, Director, OSU-CVM Clinical Skills Program at allison.biddick@okstate.edu . If you are seeking a team oriented, enjoyable working environment, Oklahoma State University's College of Veterinary Medicine is the place to be! Required Qualifications D.V.M. (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) A DVM or equivalent is required as well as at least two years of clinical experience in small animal general practice or small animal emergency. Certifications, Registrations, and/or Licenses: Eligibility for faculty licensure in Oklahoma is required. Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: The applicant should possess excellent written and non-written communication skills, be committed to promoting a welcoming and team-oriented approach to teaching and is expected to prioritize collegiality and cooperation. The ability to build meaningful professional relationships and to contribute to a friendly and enjoyable working environment is highly valued by OSU-CVM. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert f44b9a5c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Stillwater, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Stillwater OSU-Stillwater Minimum Education Level Other professional degree Other professional degree First Name (required) dc68a7f1 Last Name (required) bf36ecf6 Email (required) 9b3ba4bc Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) a15123eb Last Name (required) aa0251e3 Email (required) 11ce91b3 Save this job for later 91e6c848 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you You may also be interested in Associate Professor AF7807 Stillwater COLLEGE OF VETERINARY MEDICINE (STW) Clinical-Track Assistant/Associate Professor - Anatomic Pathology AF7881 Stillwater COLLEGE OF VETERINARY MEDICINE (STW) Tenure or Career Track Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (SA Specialist) AF7991 Stillwater COLLEGE OF VETERINARY MEDICINE (STW) Apply Now! First Name (required) 992f4192 Las